  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The 153 flat, non-slow test files of `crates/motion/tests/` move into ten domain directory suites:\n  - `adaptive2d` (17 modules)\n  - `contour2d` (20)\n  - `machining2d` (22)\n  - `holes` (13)\n  - `entry_links` (12)\n  - `machining3d` (16)\n  - `finishing3d` (13)\n  - `multiaxis` (14)\n  - `turning` (20)\n  - `edges_edm` (6)\n- Each suite has a `main.rs` that declares one module for each former file.\n- The `SLOW_BINARIES` `finish3d`, `pivot5d` and `flow` stay flat binaries. Batch still skips them, and release still runs them.\n- `rest_adaptive` and `rotary_flow` were directory suites before. They do not change.\n- `camcraft-motion` now has 15 test binaries. Before this change it had 158.\n- The files move with `git mv`. Git shows most of them as pure renames. In 14 moved files, one or two lines change:\n  - Five `mod common;` lines become `use crate::common;`. The suite root declares `common` one time.\n  - The three `adaptive_troch_*` files share `common/adaptive_troch.rs`. The `adaptive2d` root declares it one time as `fixtures`. Clippy `duplicate_mod` refuses three copies in one binary. Their two ignore reasons now name the `motion heavy: adaptive2d` step.\n  - `arc_turn_kinds`, `adaptive_orbit_seam` and `rotary_adaptive` get a `../` prefix on one `#[path]` or `include_str!`. `tests/fixtures/` and `tests/rotary_adaptive_fixture/` stay in place, because the lib unit tests also read them.\n  - Two regenerate commands in doc comments name the new suite.\n- The Gate map paragraphs stay in the modules. The gate reads them through the suite root (#3186).\n- xtask: two live-tree tests named old binaries. Now they name the suites that hold `arcs` (`contour2d`) and `cross_invariance` (`holes`). This is an expected change.\n- `docs/MACHINE-ONBOARDING.md`: the links to moved files point to the new paths.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3189-fold-motion-suites.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach flat file was a separate test binary. Each binary links the full crate again. The issue measured 4.03 GB for one target set (#919).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `motion_tests_fold_into_at_most_sixteen_binaries` (xtask, `directory_selection_tests.rs`). The pin reads the live tree. It checks that motion has at most 16 test binaries, and that each motion slow binary is still a flat file.\n  - Red on unchanged upstream/main c79c9b24f: `158 motion test binaries (at most 16)`.\n  - Green after the fold (15 binaries).\n- Test counts, `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests -- --list`:\n  - before: 2014 tests, 78 ignored (`--list --ignored`);\n  - after: 2014 tests, 78 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests` (all binaries, debug, 6 test threads): all green, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: 12 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (19.4 min). It ran the ten new suites and the xtask unit tests.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on the final head: 9 steps (release build and 8 `motion heavy:` suites), 0 failed, 0 stalled (9.0 min). `edges_edm` and `turning` have no ignored tests, so they have no heavy step.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` stops on `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67` (`needless_bool`). This PR does not change that file; its text is the same as on upstream/main. xtask is not in the gate clippy list.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. This PR changes no generator code, and no test writes a golden. I did not run `example_catalog`: it is an app suite, and this PR does not change app or any generator.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `cargo xtask gate batch`. The issue names it in \"Done means\". I ran the quick tier (all ten new suites) and the motion heavy lanes. The post-merge gate runs batch on main.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`. The heavy run covers the full tests of the light twins.\n- Disk and build time saving: not measured on this machine.\n- Wall time: some suites are now long in debug. In the quick gate (16 test threads) `adaptive2d` took 190 s, `entry_links` 167 s and `machining3d` 96 s. Batch runs suites in parallel lanes. No single test changed. The decision record says how to split a suite that proves too slow.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs change files that this PR moves. They change other lines, not the same functions. Git rename detection can carry their edits to the new paths. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #4379 (`rotary.rs`)\n- #4316 (`center_cut_owed.rs`)\n- #4173 (`chamfer_*`, `climb_direction.rs`, `deburr.rs`, and a new `chamfer_circular/leads.rs`: that support directory must move to `edges_edm/chamfer_circular/`)\n- #3103 (draft: several files, and a new flat `bore_helix.rs`, which must join the `holes` suite)\n- #4328 and #4383 add `kernel_laws` and change `common/`. They do not change the moved files.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3189\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
